From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Michael C. Ferguson" <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:35:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] zaparoo_scanout: drop the hard-coded kernel release check

validate_platform() refuses to load unless utsname()->release equals the
literal "6.18.38-MiSTer", so the module returns -ENODEV on any other
kernel even when it was built against that kernel. Module vermagic
already ties a .ko to the kernel it was compiled for, and the remaining
machine-compatible and MiSTer_fb device-tree checks still pin the
platform and the physical layout the slots depend on.

Upstream: not submitted
Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
 kernel/scanout-slots/zaparoo_scanout.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/scanout-slots/zaparoo_scanout.c b/kernel/scanout-slots/zaparoo_scanout.c
index eac3033..47811b3 100644
--- a/kernel/scanout-slots/zaparoo_scanout.c
+++ b/kernel/scanout-slots/zaparoo_scanout.c
@@ -54,8 +54,7 @@ static int validate_platform(void)
 	const __be32 *cells;
 	int len, ret = -ENODEV;
 
-	if (strcmp(utsname()->release, ZAPAROO_SCANOUT_KERNEL_RELEASE) ||
-	    !of_machine_is_compatible(ZAPAROO_SCANOUT_MACHINE))
+	if (!of_machine_is_compatible(ZAPAROO_SCANOUT_MACHINE))
 		return -ENODEV;
 	cells = of_get_property(of_root, "#address-cells", &len);
 	if (!cells || len != 4 || be32_to_cpup(cells) != 1)
-- 
2.53.0

